SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The wwccssxxffrrmm() function conforms to ISO/IEC 9899:1999 (“ISO C99”).

BBUUGGSS
     The current implementation of wwccssxxffrrmm() only works in single-byte
     LC_CTYPE locales, and falls back to using wwccssnnccppyy() in locales with ex‐
     tended character sets.

     Comparing two strings using wwccssccmmpp() after wwccssxxffrrmm() is _n_o_t always equiv‐
     alent to comparison with wwccssccoollll(); wwccssxxffrrmm() only stores information
     about primary collation weights into _d_s_t, whereas wwccssccoollll() compares
     characters using both primary and secondary weights.

